# SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
#
# description: httpServe type-checks and compiles with a named string->string handler
# mode: ir-only

# The bare-statement form is the canonical way to run a server: httpServe is registered as a
# statement-level builtin (see compilerBuiltins), so it lowers through the builtin-call codegen
# rather than being dispatched as an external command. Runtime serving behaviour is covered by
# the net-layer round-trip in src/net/HttpServer_test.cpp; this asserts the language front-end
# accepts and lowers the call (regression guard for it previously being an "Undefined function").

let handler path = "you asked for " + path

httpServe 8080 handler
